{"name":"Tiara Jewel","hex":"#eae0e8","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"tiara","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The three-tiered papal crown.","An ornamental coronet."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To adorn as a tiara.","To adorn with a tiara."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/tiara"},{"term":"jewel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A precious or semi-precious stone; gem, gemstone.","A valuable object used for personal ornamentation, especially one made of precious metals and stones; a piece of jewellery."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To bejewel; to decorate or bedeck with jewels or gems."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/jewel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tiara","blocks":[{"text":"A tiara is a head ornament adorned with jewels. Its origins date back to ancient Persia, from where it was later popularized by the Greco-Roman world. By the 18th century, the tiara had become fashionable in Europe as prestigious pieces of jewelry worn by women on formal occasions. The basic shape of the modern tiara is a semicircular base, usually made of gold, silver, or platinum, and richly decorated with gemstones, pearls, or cameos."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d8/%C3%89vrard_e_fr%C3%A9d%C3%A9ric_bapst%2C_diadema_della_duchessa_d%27anguoleme%2C_smeraldi%2C_diamanti%2C_oro_e_argento%2C_parigi_1819-20.jpg/330px-%C3%89vrard_e_fr%C3%A9d%C3%A9ric_bapst%2C_diadema_della_duchessa_d%27anguoleme%2C_smeraldi%2C_diamanti%2C_oro_e_argento%2C_parigi_1819-20.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiara","wikidata":"Q749249"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Arvstorhertiginnan_St%C3%A9phanie_av_Luxemburg.jpg/120px-Arvstorhertiginnan_St%C3%A9phanie_av_Luxemburg.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org